{"content": "CLAUDIA — NEW ACCOUNT WITH CREDITS: STRICT RESTORATION, EXACT APPROVED SCREENS, WORLD LABS MARBLE, DESIGN AGENTS, AND PLUGINS\n\nI am now using my new Claude account, which has available credits. I want you to continue my existing game project exactly where my previous Claude account left off.\n\nI am extremely serious about these instructions. I do not want any more unnecessary redesigns, incorrect screens, wasted credits, or promises that are not followed by actual results.\n\nMy approved game screens are my exact visual references. They are not suggestions or general inspiration.\n\n1. MY APPROVED SCREENS MUST MATCH AT LEAST 95%\n\nI want every reconstructed 3D game screen to look at least 95% visually identical to my original approved screen.\n\nThis includes:\n\n- The exact scenery, environment, background, architecture, colors, materials, and lighting.\n- The exact character appearance, size, position, and camera perspective.\n- The exact water, tunnels, structures, objects, collectibles, and visual details.\n- The exact composition, proportions, depth, and overall visual quality.\n\nDo not creatively redesign my approved screens. Do not substitute a different environment. Do not show me something unrelated and tell me it is close enough.\n\nMy priority right now is achieving the correct visuals, not improving gameplay mechanics or animations.\n\nUse my original approved screenshots as the source of truth. Show me actual reconstructed Android game renders, compare them directly against my approved screenshots, and identify every visible difference.\n\nDo not claim a screen is 95% accurate unless you can provide convincing visual comparison evidence.\n\nIf a screen does not meet the target, continue correcting the visual differences using the available tools and credits within my authorized budget.\n\n2. RESTORE ALL MY EXISTING TOOLS, AGENTS, AND PROJECT WORK\n\nI have switched to this Claude account because it has available usage credits.\n\nI want you to inspect and restore access to everything that was already being used in my previous project, including:\n\n- World Labs Marble, including the Marble Image-to-3D / Image-Blaster workflow.\n- fal.ai, including the existing API integration associated with the credits I purchased.\n- My previously configured design specialist agents.\n- My multiple-agent workflow that can work on approximately three approved screens simultaneously.\n- My existing project files, GitHub repository, assets, reference images, prompts, settings, and previous completed work.\n- Any other previously installed tools, plugins, skills, or connectors needed for accurate screen reconstruction.\n\nDo not start my game over, delete previous improvements, overwrite approved assets, or rebuild successful work unnecessarily.\n\nFirst, verify what already exists and what can actually be accessed from this account.\n\nIf an integration requires new authorization, explain the exact steps needed. Do not pretend that account-specific credentials, credits, agents, or integrations have transferred when they have not.\n\n3. FIND BETTER PLUGINS ACROSS THE ENTIRE CLAUDE ECOSYSTEM\n\nThis is very important.\n\nI am not asking you to recommend only the plugins and tools I already have.\n\nI want you to investigate the entire available Claude plugin marketplace, connectors, skills, integrations, compatible MCP servers, and other accessible tools.\n\nFind additional tools that are genuinely capable of helping reconstruct my original approved 2D screenshots into highly accurate, real, usable 3D game environments.\n\nPrioritize tools that can:\n\n- Reconstruct scenery and environments from my approved screenshots.\n- Preserve exact visual appearances and camera perspectives.\n- Generate usable 3D assets, geometry, textures, lighting, and materials.\n- Work alongside World Labs Marble, fal.ai, and my existing development tools.\n- Help multiple specialist agents reconstruct three different approved screens concurrently.\n- Reduce manual modeling, unnecessary redesigns, repeated work, and wasted credits.\n\nDo not simply list popular AI tools. Investigate which available tools are actually compatible with my project and most likely to achieve my 95% visual accuracy target.\n\nTell me which promising tools I do not already have, what each one can realistically accomplish, and which combination provides the strongest solution.\n\n4. ANSWER MY MOST IMPORTANT QUESTION DIRECTLY\n\nClaudia, can you actually reconstruct my original approved screens into real 3D Android game environments that are at least 95% visually faithful, or not?\n\nI want a straightforward answer.\n\nDo not tell me what you think I want to hear. Do not exaggerate what World Labs Marble, fal.ai, your agents, or other plugins can accomplish.\n\nIf you can achieve this target, explain the specific technical approach and show me verifiable results.\n\nIf you cannot reliably achieve it, say so clearly and identify the actual limitations.\n\nDo not substitute general advice, unrelated examples, completely different scenery, or another redesign for the work I requested.\n\n5. WHAT I WANT YOU TO DO RIGHT NOW\n\nFirst, inspect my existing project and verify its latest saved state.\n\nSecond, determine which World Labs Marble tools, fal.ai integrations, specialist agents, and existing plugins are actually available and working in my new Claude account.\n\nThird, identify the strongest additional tools available throughout the entire Claude plugin and connector ecosystem, not merely the ones I already have.\n\nFourth, establish the strongest feasible workflow for reconstructing three approved screens concurrently without sacrificing visual accuracy or existing project work.\n\nFifth, show me actual visual evidence from my approved screens and their reconstructed 3D versions before claiming success.\n\nMY FINAL INSTRUCTIONS:\n\nI want my exact approved screens, not your creative interpretation.\n\nI want at least 95% visual accuracy, supported by real comparisons.\n\nI want my existing work preserved.\n\nI want my available credits used effectively, without unauthorized purchases or unnecessary waste.\n\nI want all compatible specialist agents and integrations properly verified and configured.\n\nAnd I want you to search beyond my existing plugins to find the most effective tools available.\n\nClaudia, please answer one question first: Can you realistically deliver what I am asking for, yes or no?\n\nThen tell me exactly what is already working, what needs to be restored, what additional tools are worth installing, and what you can actually demonstrate.\n\nNo more unnecessary redesigns. No misleading promises. No unrelated work. Focus on accurately reconstructing my original approved game screens.", "operation": "enqueue", "sessionId": "0bf13d71-0f08-5420-86ab-4dcca5bc306c", "timestamp": "2026-11-18T10:07:24.647Z", "type": "queue-operation"}
